  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wt500.html",
  "prefLabel": "Env-Wt 511.08 Deck or Patio Repair Project Classifications",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wt 511.08 Deck or Patio Repair Project Classifications.\n\n(a) Repair of an existing deck or patio shall be a minimum impact project only if all of the following criteria are met:\n\n(1) The deck or patio is an existing legal structure; and\n\n(2) No work is done in a wetland, watercourse, or PRA, except as provided in Env-Wt 407.\n\n(b) Repair of an existing deck or patio shall be a minor impact project if the criteria of (a), above, are not met.\n\n(c) A deck or patio that is not an existing legal structure shall not be repaired unless an after-the-fact permit is obtained for the construction of the structure, which shall be classified as provided in Env-Wt 511.06.\n\nSource. #12805, eff 12-15-19; amd by #12954, eff 12-24-19; ss by #13124, eff 10-23-20; ss by #13776, eff 10-13-23",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wt500.html"
